      "title": "Verify replacement endpoints before retiring the faulty release",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "After replacement readiness and a verified JSON prediction/version response, stop and remove only the faulty test release, preserving the approved replacement.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f7"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Send a JSON request body as encoded bytes in urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}, method=\"POST\"), then read the response through urlopen with a stated timeout.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f8"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Serialize structured request/response values with json.dumps; decode JSON with json.loads before inspecting fields.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f9"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Inspect the running container identity and State, including Health when a healthcheck is configured, and compare them with the intended release.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb5"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f10"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Inspect runtime logs for initialization and execution failures without copying sensitive request data or credentials into the evidence record.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb5"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f11"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Call the declared readiness and prediction endpoints with bounded timeouts and check the returned status and payload against the expected contracts.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
