      "title": "Trace the approved rollback replacement",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Keep the faulty test release running while starting the approved previous release under its distinct identity and published port. Resolve the recorded immutable artifact rather than latest. Inspect replacement State, available Health and sanitized logs. With bounded calls, verify readiness and decoded JSON prediction/version against the contract. Only then stop and remove the faulty test release, preserving the replacement. Keep credentials runtime-injected, not in image metadata, Compose values or evidence.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#tb6"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f1",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f2",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f3",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f4",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f5",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f6",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f7",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f8",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f9",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f10",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f11",
              "mle.model_release_rollback#f12"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Rollback is not ‘use latest’ or remove everything old. The target must retain its approval/version identity, and the faulty test release is not retired before replacement readiness.",
          "role": "misconception",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
