          "items": [
            {
              "item_id": "item1",
              "text": "Verified transition\n```\nB initially remains running. Start prediction-A from approved fixture.local/orders@sha256:29371dd36fb111803c6fe996426f342680170dec59168e1e52139cdb4fbfaf83 with required nonsecret environment, runtime-injected secret and distinct published host port 8081. Inspect intended identity, Running State and Health where configured; sanitized logs show no initialization/execution failure. GET readiness within 2.0 seconds checks status and decoded state; POST encoded JSON with application/json and same timeout checks decoded version A and predictions [5.0, 8.0, 11.0]. Only after both verification checks pass: stop and remove prediction-B. Approved A remains running; evidence contains no credentials or sensitive request data.\n```"
            },
            {
              "item_id": "item2",
              "text": "Early retirement\n```\nStop and remove prediction-B before checking replacement readiness or prediction/version response. Then start A and assume it is ready.\n```"
            },
            {
              "item_id": "item3",
              "text": "Wrong replacement identity\n```\nLaunch the A container name but use faulty B artifact fixture.local/orders@sha256:cb8f33490a33bce2025fd396588bde12c4f8822336c379bcc96449329c5762ce. Prediction response confirms version B. Verdict says approved A restored.\n```"
            },
            {
              "item_id": "item4",
              "text": "Secret leak\n```\nRelease configuration embeds credential literal in Dockerfile ENV; evidence includes protected request values. Runtime secret injection is bypassed.\n```"
            }
          ]
